# Whitelist: ignore the whole context, then re-include only what the image needs.
# The Dockerfile copies exactly these: both pyproject.toml files, uv.lock, the PyPI overview,
# the package sources and the license/notice pair. Anything new (docs, samples, tests, .venv, .git, ...)
# stays out by default and has to be opted in here explicitly.

*

!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!docs/pypi-overview.md
!baycone
!baycone_cli
!service
!LICENSE
!NOTICE

# Re-exclude caches living inside the whitelisted source tree.
# .dockerignore matches Go path patterns, not gitignore globs, so nested paths
# need an explicit '**/'. The last matching pattern wins, so this must come
# after the package re-includes above.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
